From e4642c8e8694cc22afa01fb5186fbe83a9d7d65f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:06:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] perf(motion): skip blocked doors in the adaptive routed
 return

The 2D Adaptive plan at optimal_load 0.5 on the box part of #2736 took
29.6 s in release, and 16 s of it was the door search of routed
microlift returns. A door from a point whose own disc holds stock
read the leg law on every free cell within 6 mm (0.05 mm grid), and
could never pass: every leg's capsule holds its start disc.

The door search now refuses such a point before any leg is read, and
reads the other candidates nearest first. The chosen cell is the same
(nearest legal cell, lower index on a tie): output is identical by
hash on nine region and load cases. The plan takes 9.8 s in release
and 60 s in debug.

Fixes #2736

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
